Rubypp is a preprocessor that uses ruby to transform text.  Syntax is
similar to the C preprocessor, e.g.:

#include <stdio.h>

#ruby <<END
  a = 42
  nil # the last value of the block gets inserted into the output stream
END

int main()
{
  printf("The answer is: #{a}\n");
}

